course: dictionary
lesson: 1139
title: Brewery: a place or a company
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. «Joseph Priestley found how to put gas into water and made the first soda water, using gas from a brewery; he also discovered oxygen, as Carl Scheele did on his own.» Here a brewery is the building where beer is made, because gas comes from a place.
explain: Brewery has two meanings: a factory or building where beer is made, or a company that makes beer. The ending -ery often names a place, as in bakery, so a brewery is most often a building. When you read «the brewery sent a lorry of beer to every pub», the job of sending beer tells you it means the company.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If "a factory where beer is made" still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Brewery is a noun: one brewery, two breweries.
fact: «Brewery» means a factory or building where beer is made, or a company that makes beer.
fact: Joseph Priestley used gas from a brewery to make the first soda water.
fact: Towns often grew up around breweries, so a brewery could be the heart of a town.
fact: Brewery horses are large, strong horses that pulled beer carts, and you can see them at shows in the UK.
exercise: «Joseph Priestley made soda water using gas from a brewery.» What is a brewery here? | A kind of cold drink | *A factory or building where beer is made | A river bank | A school for beer tasters
exercise: «The brewery sent a lorry of beer to every pub in town.» What does brewery mean here? | A horse that pulls carts | A building with a tall tower | *A company that makes beer | A bottle of soda water
exercise: A brewery and a bakery both end in -ery. What does this ending often show? | A number | A sound | A feeling | *A place where something is made or done
test: What is the plural of brewery? | brewerys | brewerees | *breweries | brewries
test: «Priestley's soda water used gas from a brewery.» What did the gas come from? | A river | A school | A shop selling sweets | *A factory where beer is made
exam: The word «brewery» can mean a building or a company. Which sentence uses it to mean a company? | «The old brewery had a big red door and a tall chimney.» | *«The brewery signed a deal with a supermarket to sell its beer across the country.» | «She put the brewery in her bag for lunch.»
